# Prisma

## Prisma 7 setup (project-specific)

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Config | Database URL in `prisma.config.ts` — **not** in `schema.prisma` |
| Client output | `src/generated/prisma` via `generator output` in schema |
| Dev adapter | `src/lib/db.ts` uses `@prisma/adapter-better-sqlite3` |
| Prod swap | See `docs/postgresql.md` — change adapter + `datasource provider` |
| Singleton | `globalForPrisma` pattern in `db.ts` — do not create multiple `PrismaClient` instances |
| Env | `DATABASE_URL` validated in `src/env.ts` |

## Schema conventions

- Both sides of every `@relation` with `@relation` attribute
- `@@map` / `@map` for Better Auth table names (`user`, `session`, `account`, etc.)
- Org models: `Organization`, `Member`, `Invitation` — all org-scoped queries filter by `organizationId`
- Session field `activeOrganizationId` on `Session` — set on signup hook and org switch
- Timestamps: `createdAt` + `updatedAt` where applicable
- Indexes on foreign keys (`@@index([userId])`, `@@index([organizationId])`)

## Commands

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Fresh local DB | `pnpm bootstrap` or `pnpm db:push` |
| Migrations | `pnpm db:migrate` (fresh clones); existing DB may need baseline — see `.cursor/context.md` |
| Generate client | `pnpm db:generate` (runs on `postinstall`) |

## Query rules

- Use Prisma ORM — parameterized queries only; no raw SQL string concatenation
- Org-scoped reads/writes: always include `organizationId` from verified session
- Use `prisma.member.findFirst({ where: { userId, organizationId } })` for membership checks — prefer `tenant-guard.ts` helpers
- **NEVER** delete Better Auth core models (`User`, `Session`, `Account`, `Verification`) — extend, don't replace

## Cross-reference

> For IDOR prevention and RBAC, see `better-auth-multitenancy.mdc` and `security.mdc`.
